--
--
N5008 [expr.prim.fold] in a trailing-return-type decltype with a
pack instantiated at size >= 2.  Reducing the fold in typecheck_type
would need the replicated `<base>$k` value parameters, which are only
created during the called specialization's own body instantiation and
are not in scope while the trailing return type is checked.  CBMC
drops the whole declaration ("found no match for symbol 'sum'").  The
size-0/1 cases are fixed (see cpp17_fold_in_trailing_decltype);
accepted by g++/clang -std=c++17.

ROUND-126: root-cause chain of the SHARED ranges/__bind_back failure
fully mapped (see b79138d38c):
 1. declaration+definition of the same function template each get a
    template scope; typecheck_function_template seeds
    pack_size_map[<scope>::<pack>]=0 per scope;
 2. after the [temp.over.link]/6 merge the superseded scope's zero is
    read as "genuinely empty pack" and the empty-pack strip removes
    `std::forward<_Args>(__args)...` from the stored trailing-return
    decltype -> "<<type:auto>>" at every call (FIXED: seeds purged +
    scope detached on merge);
 3. REMAINING: the deduction-time speculative instantiation registers
    the skeleton's parameters in the ENCLOSING NAMESPACE
    (convert_non_template_declaration under
    guess_function_template_args creates scope entry `std::__args`),
    so after the merge `__args` resolves ambiguously ("does not
    uniquely resolve").  The leak exists in the single-declaration
    case too, where it is masked.  redecl.cpp is the 50-line
    header-free reproducer (declaration+definition pair).
NEXT: quarantine the deduction skeleton's parameter registration (a
guessed-conversion under guess_function_template_args must not
register ids in the enclosing namespace scope, or must remove them
when the speculation completes).
